pimsync synchronises calendars and contacts between different storages,
including plain local directories and remote CalDAV, CardDAV and Webcal
servers.

Collections can be grouped into pairs, a single storage may take part in
more than one pair, and conflicting modifications are detected and reported
instead of being silently overwritten. Synchronisation can be run once or
continuously in daemon mode.

pimsync is the successor and a reimplementation of vdirsyncer.
